From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:06:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-spm-sleep: optionally skip the SODI
 idle state

With 0816 or 0817 loaded on an image with CONFIG_CPU_IDLE, SODI test
periods stopped returning under inbound pings and the device reset
(stages D5a, D5b). The 0806 module passed the same test on that image
(D5c). The cpuidle driver registration is the largest difference left.

Add sodi_idle (default on): when off at load, the CPU0 cpuidle driver
is not registered, and the rest of the module is unchanged.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
index 9599a3c0d..549f37466 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
@@ -1157,6 +1157,11 @@ static unsigned int sodi_idle_max_ms = 2000;
 module_param(sodi_idle_max_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(sodi_idle_max_ms, "SODI idle: longest period in ms (1-2000)");
 
+/* Whether to register the cpuidle driver at all (stage D5d bisects it) */
+static bool sodi_idle = true;
+module_param(sodi_idle, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(sodi_idle, "SODI idle: register the CPU0 cpuidle driver");
+
 static const u8 sodi_wake_bit[] = { 0, 2, 5, 6, 22 };
 static const char * const sodi_wake_name[] = {
 	"timer", "keypad", "conn2ap", "eint", "cirq",
@@ -1368,7 +1373,7 @@ static void sodi_idle_register(void)
 	struct device_node *np;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CPU_IDLE) || !s.sodi.ready)
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CPU_IDLE) || !sodi_idle || !s.sodi.ready)
 		return;
 	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "pwm-backlight");
 	s.bl = np ? of_find_backlight_by_node(np) : NULL;
-- 
2.43.0

